-- title:
--   Ends other than O escape the branch Wₓ
-- statement:
--   **Setting.** Let $q$ be a prime and $M'$ a non-zero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell \mid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero, $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity, and assume (`hι`) that there is a ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\zeta) = e^{2\pi i/q}$. Let $H_1$ be a subgroup of $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ equal (`hH₁`) to $\mathrm{levelH}(q,M') \cap \ker\big((\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/\ell)^\times\big)$, where [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22) is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$; thus $H_1$ consists of the units congruent to $1$ both modulo $q$ and modulo $\ell$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}(L)$ equal (`hK`) to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') H₁)`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. the $L$-subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(L)$ generated by the image under coefficientwise extension $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\mathbb{Q}) \to \mathrm{LaurentSeries}(L)$ of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$.
--
--   Let $A$ be a henselian discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L$ and algebraically closed residue field, with $q \in \mathfrak{m}_A$ (`hAq`) and with $\zeta$ in the image of $A$ (`hζA`), and let $K$ be an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$. Let $j \in K$ be non-zero with Laurent series equal (`hj`) to the image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157), the $q$-expansion $q^{-1} + 744 + \cdots$ of the modular $j$-function. Let $\varpi$ generate $\mathfrak{m}_A$ (`hϖ`), and let $\varpi_t \in A$ satisfy $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q\,u$ for some unit $u$ (`hϖt`). Throughout, `chartAlgFin A K j` denotes the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ of elements integral over $A[j]$, `jChartFin A K j` denotes $j$ viewed in it, and [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) denotes the scheme obtained as the pushout glueing $\mathrm{Spec}$ of this algebra to $\mathrm{Spec}$ of the corresponding algebra for $j^{-1}$, with its structure morphism `toBase` to $\mathrm{Spec}\,A$ and its chart immersion `ιFin` from `XFin A K j = Spec (chartAlgFin A K j)`.
--
--   **Supersingularity of the centre.** Let $y$ be a maximal ideal of `chartAlgFin A K j` containing $\varpi$ (`hy`, `hϖy`), and assume (`hss`) that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from `chartAlgFin A K j` to $\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the element $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), the set of those $j$-invariants for which every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with that invariant has no non-zero point killed by $q$.
--
--   **The Drinfeld-chart rigidity package `hArig`.** This hypothesis asserts: for every point $z$ of the two-chart integral model, for $\varpi_z$ the germ at $z$ of the global section obtained from $\varpi$ along `toBase` (`hϖz`) lying in the maximal ideal of the stalk at $z$ (`hz`), for every point $y'$ of `XFin A K j` with `ιFin` image $z$ (`hy'`) such that the supersingularity condition above holds with $y$ replaced by the prime of $y'$ (`hss'`), there exist a complete discrete valuation domain $W$, a ring homomorphism $\sigma : A \to W$ with $\mathfrak{m}_W = (\sigma\varpi)$, power series $f,u,v \in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u,v$ units and $f \equiv X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1 \pmod{(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}}$ (the residual Drinfeld form), and a ring isomorphism
--   $$e : \widehat{\mathcal{O}}_{z} \;\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }\; S := W[[X_0,X_1]]/\big(\mathrm{C}(\sigma(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))\,v - f\,u\big)$$
--   from the adic completion of the stalk at $z$, such that, writing $\mathrm{toC}$ for the map from the stalk to its completion, $\mathrm{mkS}$ for the quotient map onto $S$, and $\mathrm{germY}$ for the ring map from `chartAlgFin A K j` to the stalk at $z$ given by the germ at $z$ on the open image of `ιFin` composed with the inverses of the relevant affine comparison isomorphisms, the following seven conjuncts hold.
--
--   (1) *Constants*: for all $a \in A$, $e$ of the germ of $a$ equals the class of $\mathrm{C}(\sigma a)$.
--
--   (2) *Chart stability*: for every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and every $\tau \in \mathrm{Aut}_L(K)$ with `IsLevelAutAt L q ζ q (q^2*M') H₁ γ⁻¹ K τ` — that is, for all weights $k$, all weight-$k$ modular forms $f,g$ for $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ with integral $q$-expansions $p_f,p_g$, $p_g \neq 0$, all $x \in K$ whose Laurent series is the image of $p_f/p_g$, and all $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\zeta) = e^{2\pi i /q}$, one has $\iota(\tau x) \cdot \mathrm{qExp}(g\mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,q\,\gamma^{-1}) = \mathrm{qExp}(f\mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,q\,\gamma^{-1})$ — the automorphism $\tau$ maps `chartAlgFin A K j` into itself.
--
--   (3) *Trivial diamond fixes $y'$*: for such $\gamma$ with $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \pmod \ell$ and such $\tau$ preserving the chart algebra, $\tau(a) - a$ lies in the prime of $y'$ for every $a$ in the chart algebra.
--
--   (4) *Linearisation*: for such $\gamma$ and $\tau$ preserving the chart algebra and fixing $y'$ in the above sense, there are a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, an element $c \in W$ and a matrix $M \in \mathrm{Mat}_2(W)$ with: $\theta \circ e \circ \mathrm{toC} \circ \mathrm{germY} = e \circ \mathrm{toC} \circ \mathrm{germY} \circ \tau$ on the chart algebra; $\theta$ fixing all constants $\mathrm{C}(w)$; $\theta(X_j) \equiv \sum_i M_{ij}X_i$ modulo the square of the ideal generated by the classes of $X_0,X_1$; $c^{q+1} \equiv 1$, $M_{ij} \equiv c\,\gamma_{ij} \pmod{\mathfrak{m}_W}$; $c \equiv 1 \pmod{\mathfrak{m}_W}$ whenever $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \pmod \ell$; and $c \not\equiv 1 \pmod{\mathfrak{m}_W}$ whenever $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \neq \mathrm{id}$.
--
--   (5) *Separation of branches*: for integers $a_1,b_1,a_2,b_2$ and primes $P_1,P_2$ of $S$, each containing the class of $\mathrm{C}(\sigma\varpi)$, each failing to contain at least one of the classes of $X_0,X_1$, and each containing an element of the shape $a_iX_0 + b_iX_1 + h_i$ with $h_i \in (X_0,X_1)^2$, if $q \nmid a_1b_2 - a_2b_1$ then the contractions of $P_1$ and $P_2$ along $e \circ \mathrm{toC}$ are distinct.
--
--   (6) *Integrality criterion along a branch*: for a prime $P$ of $S$ containing the class of $\mathrm{C}(\sigma\varpi)$, not containing both classes of $X_0,X_1$, and containing $X_0 + h$ for some $h \in (X_0,X_1)^2$: an element $a$ of the chart algebra satisfies $\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}(a)) \in (e)^{-1}P$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$ lies in the image of $\mathfrak{m}_A$.
--
--   (7) *The series $j(q\tau)$*: [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L q`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) — the Laurent series obtained from the $j$-expansion by multiplying all exponents by $q$ — lies in $K$ and in the chart algebra, and there are $a_0 \in A$ with $\mathrm{jqNModC} - a_0$ in the prime of $y'$, an integer $e_0 \geq 1$ and $h \in (X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ such that for all $a,b \in W$ not both in $\mathfrak{m}_W$ with $a^qb - ab^q \in \mathfrak{m}_W$ the sum $\sum_{i=0}^{e_0} \mathrm{coeff}_{(i,e_0-i)}(h)\,a^ib^{e_0-i}$ is a unit, and $e(\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}(\mathrm{jqNModC}-a_0))) = \mathrm{mkS}(h)$.
--
--   **The fixed point and its chart witness.** Fix $z$, $\varpi_z$ (`hϖz`, `hz`), $y'$ (`hy'`, `hss'`) as above, with the prime of $y'$ equal to $y$ (`hy'y`). Fix also data $W_1, \sigma_1, f_1, u_1, v_1$ (with $u_1,v_1$ units, `hσ₁` giving $\mathfrak{m}_{W_1} = (\sigma_1\varpi)$, `hf₁` the congruence to the Drinfeld form modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$) and an isomorphism $e_1$ of the completed stalk with $S = W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/(\mathrm{C}(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{q+1}))v_1 - f_1u_1)$, and assume (`hW₁`) the conjuncts (1)–(7) above verbatim for this witness at $(z,y')$.
--
--   **Blow-up ideal, blow-up chart and its properties.** Let $J$ be the ideal of `chartAlgFin A K j` given (`hJ`) as the infimum of all ideals of the form $\tau^{-1}\big((e_1 \circ \mathrm{toC} \circ \mathrm{germY})^{-1}\,(\mathrm{mkS}(\mathrm{C}(\sigma_1\varpi_t)), \mathrm{mkS}(X_0), \mathrm{mkS}(X_1))\big)$, where $\gamma$ runs over $\Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ over the automorphisms with `IsLevelAutAt … γ⁻¹ K τ` preserving the chart algebra. Let $B$ be the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ generated (`hB`) over `chartAlgFin A K j` by $\{x \in K : x\varpi_t \in J\}$, and let $W$ be a valuation subring of $K$ containing $B$ (`hBW`). Assume:
--
--   `hR1`: `chartAlgFin A K j` $\leq B$, and every $f \in K$ is of the form $g/h$ with $g,h \in B$, $h \neq 0$.
--
--   `hR2`: $A \to B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation, and $B/\varpi B$ has Krull dimension at most $1$.
--
--   `hR3` (five clauses): $W \cap L$ is exactly the image of $A$; $\mathfrak{m}_W$ is generated by $\varpi$; $W$ is a discrete valuation ring; for $b$ in the chart algebra, $b \in y$ if and only if $b \in \mathfrak{m}_W$; and $W$ is the localisation of $B$ at $\mathfrak{m}_W$, in the sense that $f \in W$ iff $f = g/h$ with $g,h \in B$ and $h \notin \mathfrak{m}_W$.
--
--   `hEQ` (five clauses): (i) for every $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$-algebra structure on the residue field of $A$ there is a surjective ring homomorphism $\rho$ from $B$ onto [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q (ResidueField A)`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) (the quotient of $(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)[X_0,X_1]$ by $\mathrm{drinfeldPoly}-1$) whose vanishing locus is exactly $\mathfrak{m}_W \cap B$, which is compatible with $A \to \mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$, and which is equivariant for level automorphisms: for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ as above preserving $W$ there are $c \in \mathbb{F}_{q^2}^\times$ with $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma, c)$ in the kernel [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) of the character $(g,c) \mapsto \det(g)c^{q+1}$ such that $\rho \circ \tau = \mathrm{hAction}(\ldots) \circ \rho$ on $B$, and $c \neq 1$ whenever $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \neq \mathrm{id}$; (ii) $B$ is stable under all such $\tau$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; (iii) every prime $Q$ of $B$ containing $\varpi$ receives the centre of $W$ under some level automorphism with $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$, in the sense that $\tau(b) \in B \cap Q$ for every $b \in B \cap \mathfrak{m}_W$; (iv) if $b \in B$ is carried into $\mathfrak{m}_W$ by every such level automorphism with $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$, then $\varpi \mid b$ in $B$; (v) any level automorphism with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ preserving $y$ on the chart algebra preserves $W$.
--
--   Assume further that [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L q`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) lies in $K$ (`hjK`) and in the chart algebra (`hjC`), and let $m \geq 1$ be such that $\varpi^m = \varpi_t w$ for a unit $w$ (`hm1`, `hmt`).
--
--   **Ends.** Let $\mathrm{ends}$ be a finite set of subrings of $K$ characterised (`hends`) by: $O \in \mathrm{ends}$ if and only if there is $a \in J$ with $a \neq 0$ in $K$ such that, setting $B_a$ to be the $A$-subalgebra generated over the chart algebra by $\{x \in K : xa \in J\}$, there is a maximal ideal $P$ of $B_a$ with: $f \in O$ iff $f = g/h$ with $g,h \in B_a$ and $h \notin P$; every $b \in y$ that lies in $O$ is a non-unit of $O$; and $O$ does not contain $B$.
--
--   Fix $O \in \mathrm{ends}$ (`hOmem`) with: $O \subseteq W$ (`hOW`), $O$ local (`hOloc`) and noetherian (`hOnoe`), and the chart algebra contained in $O$ (`hCO`). Assume $\varpi \in O$ (`hϖO`), and let $c_x, c_y \in O$, $u$ a unit of $O$, and
--   $$\iota : \widehat{O} \;\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }\; \hat{A}[[X_0,X_1]]/(X_0X_1 - \varpi^m)$$
--   a ring isomorphism of the $\mathfrak{m}_O$-adic completion of $O$ with the crossing model `UVCrossingModel` over the $\mathfrak{m}_A$-adic completion of $A$ at the parameter $\varpi^m$, together with units $\gamma_U, \gamma_V$ of that model, such that: $c_xc_y = \varpi^m u$ (`hcxy`); $\iota$ sends the image of each $a \in A$ lying in $O$ to `UVCrossingModel.const` of its image in $\hat A$ (`hιc`); $\iota(c_x) = \gamma_U \cdot \mathrm{U}$ and $\iota(c_y) = \gamma_V \cdot \mathrm{V}$ for the two distinguished elements $\mathrm{U},\mathrm{V}$ of the crossing model (`hιx`, `hιy`); $c_y \in \mathfrak{m}_W$ (`hcyW`) and $c_x \notin \mathfrak{m}_W$ (`hcxW`).
--
--   **The branch $W_x$.** Finally, let $W_x$ be a valuation subring of $K$ with: $O \subseteq W_x$ (`hB0`); the chart algebra contained in $W_x$ (`hB1`); $W_x \cap L$ exactly the image of $A$ (`hB2`); $W_x$ a discrete valuation ring (`hB3`); $\mathfrak{m}_{W_x}$ generated by $\varpi$ (`hB4`); for every polynomial $p$ over $A$, if $p$ evaluated at [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L q`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) lies in $\mathfrak{m}_{W_x}$ then all coefficients of $p$ lie in $\mathfrak{m}_A$ (`hB6`, residual transcendence of $j(q\tau)$); $c_x \in \mathfrak{m}_{W_x}$ (`hB7`) and $c_y \notin \mathfrak{m}_{W_x}$ (`hB8`); every element of the chart algebra lying in $\mathfrak{m}_{W_x}$ lies in $y$ (`hB9`); and some element of $y$ does not lie in $\mathfrak{m}_{W_x}$ (`hB10`), so that the centre of $W_x$ contracts to a prime strictly inside $y$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** For every subring $O'$ of $K$ with $O' \in \mathrm{ends}$ and $O' \neq O$ there exists $f \in K$ with $f \in O'$ and $f \notin W_x$. Equivalently: no end other than $O$ is contained in the branch $W_x$.
--
--   In the classical picture this is the separation statement for Igusa components through a supersingular point: after blowing up the tame node of the integral model, the distinct ends of the blow-up chart lie on distinct branches, so the discrete valuation ring $W_x$ singled out by the end $O$ (the branch through $O$, on which $j(q\tau)$ is residually transcendental) contains no other end. It is the form of the statement used in the auxiliary frame where the full level is replaced by the $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$-level with a guard prime $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ dividing $M'$, and it feeds the construction of the Igusa valuation subring attached to an end of the blow-up chart.
